title: Suresh_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite AutoStand>>

// Scene Setup - Auto stand encounter
While walking through the bustling auto stand, Raju stops to talk with Suresh, the friendly auto driver who always notices his cricket equipment.

The familiar chaos surrounds Raju as he approaches Suresh's bright yellow three-wheeler. This corner feels like a refuge where genuine conversation can occur.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: Arre, little champ! Always running around with that bat in your hands, haan?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: Even when you're not practicing, you carry it like it's part of your body.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Excited">>
Suresh: That's real dedication I see there, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Yes, bhaiya! I want to play cricket one day, for real.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Not just in the lanes with tennis balls, but proper cricket with leather balls.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: In stadiums, maybe even for India someday. Do you think that sounds crazy?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Sad">>
Suresh: Crazy? No, beta. Not crazy at all.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: I wanted exactly the same thing once.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: Played for my school team, even got selected for district-level camps.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Really, bhaiya? You were a serious cricketer?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: You actually played at district level? That's amazing!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: The coaches said I had natural timing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Excited">>
Suresh: Wristwork that reminded them of Mohammad Azharuddin.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's incredible, bhaiya! Azharuddin's wristwork is legendary!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: But then... why are you driving an auto now instead of playing cricket?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Sad">>
Suresh: Dreams cost money, beta. More money than families like ours usually have.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: When I was your age, my cricket was improving every month.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: Coaches were talking about state-level selections, maybe even further.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Sad">>
Suresh: But then my father got sick - really sick.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: Hospital bills, medicines, no income while he couldn't work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I'm so sorry, bhaiya. That must have been very difficult.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: Someone had to step up and support the family.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Sad">>
Suresh: Cricket doesn't feed hungry stomachs or pay medical bills. Auto driving does.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: So I chose responsibility over dreams.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Sad">>
Suresh: I've never regretted that choice, but I've never forgotten what I gave up either.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: That's a big sacrifice, bhaiya. You gave up so much.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But I'll find a way to make cricket work. I'll find scholarships, sponsors, something.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I won't let money stop me from playing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: Good, beta. Hold on to that fire - it's precious and rare.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Quizzical">>
Suresh: Just remember something important about fire.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Serious">>
Suresh: It can warm you and give you energy, but it can also burn you if you're not careful.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: Dreams are powerful, but they need to be balanced with practical wisdom.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I understand, bhaiya. I'll be smart about it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Suresh" "Smiling">>
Suresh: That's good to hear, champ. Keep that balance in mind.

<<HideCharacter>>

// Scene Conclusion
As Raju walks away, he carries both Suresh's story and his warning about balancing passion with practicality.

<<set $Suresh_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

